<Base lang="en" title="eSathi UP Login & Registration: ID, Password and OTP Help" description="Guide to eSathi UP registration, citizen login, forgotten Login ID or password recovery, OTP and captcha problems." path="/en/login-registration/" altPath="/login-registration/" faqs={faqs} updated="23 October 2026">
<div class="content-col"><h1 class="page-title">eSathi Login & Registration Help Centre</h1><p class="updated-line">The right portal, credential and fixes for common login errors</p>
<div class="warn"><strong>Stay safe:</strong> Never share an OTP, password or full Aadhaar number. Sign in only on the <a href="https://esathi.up.gov.in/citizenservices/login/login.aspx" rel="noopener" target="_blank">official eSathi portal</a>.</div>
<div class="action-grid"><a class="action-card" href="https://esathi.up.gov.in/citizenservices/login/login.aspx" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>Official Citizen Login ↗</strong><span>Register or sign in securely</span></a><a class="action-card" href="/en/status-verification/"><strong>Track without signing in</strong><span>Check progress with an application number</span></a></div>
<section class="box"><h2>Register in 3 steps</h2><div class="steps"><div class="step"><span class="step-num"></span><div class="step-body"><h3>Choose New User Registration</h3><p>Enter your name, birth date, address, district and mobile. Match identity-document spellings.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span class="step-num"></span><div class="step-body"><h3>Create a Login ID</h3><p>Choose a memorable username. It is not your mobile number; save it securely.</p></div></div><div class="step"><span class="step-num"></span><div class="step-body"><h3>Complete OTP verification</h3><p>Activate the account through the registered mobile and create a strong password.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Fix common problems</h2><table class="data"><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>First action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Invalid credentials</td><td>Use the chosen username, not your mobile; then try password recovery.</td></tr><tr><td>Captcha incorrect</td><td>Refresh it, check letter case and reset browser zoom.</td></tr><tr><td>OTP missing</td><td>Confirm the registered mobile and signal; resend after the cooldown.</td></tr><tr><td>Repeated errors</td><td>Stop retrying, use a private window, then contact the official helpdesk.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Before you register</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Keep an active mobile and email ready; follow the verification method currently shown by the portal.</li><li>Match your name, birth date and address to your primary identity record.</li><li>Store the Login ID and password in a private password manager.</li><li>Check the official domain spelling before entering credentials.</li><li>On a shared computer, do not save the password and always sign out.</li></ul></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Recover a forgotten Login ID or password</h2><h3>Forgotten Login ID</h3><ol><li>Open the recovery option on the official login page.</li><li>Enter the account details requested there and the registered mobile.</li><li>Record the ID received through the official flow. Never give the OTP to a caller or agent.</li></ol><h3>Forgotten password</h3><ol><li>Open password recovery and provide the Login ID/mobile details requested.</li><li>Verify the OTP on the official page and create a unique new password.</li><li>If the old password was reused elsewhere, change it on those services too.</li></ol><div class="note">The portal interface can change. If labels differ, use the recovery/help option visible on the official page. This guide never collects credentials.</div></section>
<section class="box"><h2>After registration: start an application</h2><ol><li>Select the relevant department and certificate from the services available after login.</li><li>Read the current document list and upload instructions before filling the form.</li><li>Review names, district, tehsil and address before submission.</li><li>Pay only the amount displayed by the portal and save the receipt/application number.</li><li>Continue with the <a href="/en/status-verification/">status and verification guide</a>.</li></ol></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Account safety</h2><ul><li>Never give a helpdesk or CSC operator your password or OTP.</li><li>Do not install a remote-access app at a caller's request.</li><li>Pay only through the gateway opened by the official portal, never a personal UPI ID.</li><li>Hide Aadhaar, mobile and transaction data before sharing an error screenshot.</li><li>Remove downloaded identity scans from a shared device after use.</li></ul></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Official helpdesk</h2><p>Government district pages list <strong>0522-2304706</strong> and <strong>ceghelpdesk@gmail.com</strong>. Share an application number when needed—never an OTP or password.</p></section></div></Base>
